\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. There were ninety and nine that safely lay
\par In the shelter of the fold;
\par But one was out on the hills away,
\par Far off from the gates of gold,
\par Away on the mountains wild and bare,
\par Away from the tender Shepherd's care.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Lord, Thou hast here Thy ninety 
\par and nine;
\par Are they not enough for Thee?
\par But the Shepherd made answer:
\par This is Mine
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Has wandered away from Me;
\par And although the road be rough
\par and steep,
\par I go to the desert to find My sheep.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. But none of the ransomed ever knew
\par How deep were the waters crossed,
\par Nor how dark was the night that 
\par the Lord passed through,
\par Ere He found His sheep that was lost.
\par Out in the desert he heard its cry,
\par Sick and helpless and ready to die.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Lord, whence are those blood-drops
\par all the way
\par That mark out the mountain's track?
\par They were shed for one who had
\par gone astray,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Ere the Shepherd could bring 
\par him back.
\par Lord, whence are Thy hands so 
\par rent and torn?
\par They are pierced to-night by 
\par many a torn.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. And all through the mountains, 
\par thunder-riven,
\par And up from the rocky steep,
\par There rose a cry to the gate of heaven:
\par Rejoice, I have found My sheep.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And the angels echoed around
\par the throne:
\par Rejoice, for the Lord brings back
\par His own.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

